> rect (2+3i)(4-5i)
(2+3i)(4-5i) = 23 + 2i
  Re = 23,  Im = 2
  check: equal numerically (23 + 2i, complex arithmetic)
> rect 1/(1+i)
1/(1+i) = 1/2 - i/2
  Re = 1/2,  Im = -1/2
  check: equal numerically (0.5 - 0.5i, complex arithmetic)
> rect i^i
i^i = exp(-pi/2)
  Re = exp(-pi/2),  Im = 0
  check: equal numerically (0.2078795764, complex arithmetic)
> re (3+4i)
Re((3+4i)) = 3
  check: equal numerically (3, complex arithmetic)
> im (3+4i)
Im((3+4i)) = 4
  check: equal numerically (4, complex arithmetic)
> conj (3+4i)
conj((3+4i)) = 3 - 4i
  check: equal numerically (3 - 4i, complex arithmetic)
> modulus (3+4i)
|(3+4i)| = 5
  check: equal numerically (5, complex arithmetic)
> arg (3+4i)
arg((3+4i)) = atan(4/3)  (about 0.927295218)
  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi
  check: equal numerically (0.927295218, complex arithmetic)
